{"data":[{"id":166,"documentId":"bwz0fp1xnzt5syif46a4sw2k","heading":"Cookie policy","slug":"cookie-policy","content":"## 1. Introduction \n\nWe use cookies and similar tracking technologies (collectively referred to as “cookies” hereinafter) when you visit our website (https://www.allwyn.com/) including any other related domain, campaign microsites operated by us, andany mobile version of the website (together “the website”).\n\nInsofar as those cookies are not strictly necessary for the provision of the website, we will ask you to consent to our use of cookies when you first visit the website.\n\nThis cookie policy is dated December 2025.\n\n## 2. What is a cookie?  \n\nA cookie is a small file containing an identifier (a string of letters and numbers) that is sent by a server to a web browser and is stored by the browser. The identifier is then sent back to the server each time the browser requests a page from the server.\n\nCookies may be either \"persistent\" cookies or \"session\" cookies: a persistent cookie will be stored by a web browser and will remain valid until its set expiry date, unless deleted by the user before the expiry date; a session cookie, on the other hand, will expire at the end of the user session, when the web browser is closed.\n\n## 3. Types of cookies that we use  \n\nOur website uses cookies and similar technologies categorised according to their purpose. These categories reflect the choices available in our cookie banner on the website and help ensure your privacy preferences are respected.\n\n- **Necessary cookies**: These cookies and similar technologies are essential for the website to function properly. They enable core features such as security, page navigation, and access to secure areas. Without these cookies, the website cannot operate correctly, and they cannot be switched off in our systems.\n- **Preferences cookies**: These cookies and similar technologies allow the website to remember information that changes the way it behaves or looks, such as your preferred language or the region you are in. They enhance your experience but are not strictly required for the website to work.\n- **Statistics cookies**: Also known as analytics cookies, these help us understand how visitors interact with the site by collecting and reporting information  in a way that does not directly identify you. This allows us to improve our website’s performance and usability over time. For example, we use statistics cookies to understand how people engage with our content and tools, including our responsible gaming games and features, so that we can improve them. \n- **Marketing cookies**: These cookies help us measure the effectiveness of our advertising and understand our user engagement by supporting services from partners such as Google, Meta and TikTok.  These technologies may record your visit to our website, including the pages you visit and links you follow. . The data collected may be used to deliver targeted advertising to you on these third-party platforms, based on your interests. The intention is to display ads that are relevant and engaging for the individual user. Information collected may be transferred outside the European Economic Area (EEA) and is subject to appropriate safeguards under applicable data protection laws.  \n\nThe responsible gaming game and similar tools on our website do not require marketing cookies to function. \n\n\n## 4. Managing Your Preferences\n\nYou can manage your cookie preferences at any time by accessing the cookie banner and setting up your preferences by clicking on “Customise”. The section ‘Details’ will provide you with a breakdown of each tracker—including its name, purpose, duration, and provider.  \n\n## 5. How to control cookies on your desktop and mobile device\n\nMost modern browsers allow you to see what cookies you have on your device and allow you to manage your preferences by using their cookie settings. The methods for doing so vary from browser to browser, and from version to version. You can, however, obtain up-to-date information about blocking and deleting cookies via these links:\n- [Chrome](https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647)  \n- [Edge](https://support.microsoft.com/en-gb/help/4468242/microsoft-edge-browsing-data-and-privacy)  \n- [Firefox](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/enhanced-tracking-protection-firefox-desktop)  \n- [Safari](https://support.apple.com/en-gb/guide/safari/manage-cookies-and-website-data-sfri11471/mac) \n- [Internet Explorer](https://support.microsoft.com/en-gb/help/17442/windows-internet-explorer-delete-manage-cookies)  \n\nHow to control cookies on your mobile device:\n- [Apple iOS Safari](https://support.apple.com/en-gb/HT201265)\n- [Android Chrome](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/61416?co=GENIE.Platform%3DAndroid&hl=en)\n\nIf you choose not to allow any cookies other than those considered strictly necessary, this may impact on your experience of the site. \n\n## 6. Our details  \n\nIf you have any questions in relation to this cookie policy, please contact the Data  Protection Officer by email at [privacy@allwyn.com](mailto:privacy@allwyn.com).  \n\n## 7. Changes to this cookie policy  \n\nWe may from time to time update this cookie policy. All key updates to this cookie policy will be published on this page. The updates will become effective on publication. We recommend that you revisit and read the cookie policy regularly to ensure that you are up to date.\n\nLast updated: December 2025","createdAt":"2025-01-27T08:45:04.008Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-29T15:30:48.833Z","publishedAt":"2026-01-29T15:30:48.813Z","locale":"en","metadata":null,"localizations":[{"id":199,"documentId":"bwz0fp1xnzt5syif46a4sw2k","heading":"Cookie policy","slug":"cookie-policy","content":"## 1. Introduction \n\nWe use cookies and similar tracking technologies (collectively referred to as “cookies”   hereinafter) when you visit our website (https://www.allwyn.com/),   including any oth